Massive volume of content on Mountain Goat Software, Scrum Alliance, Atlassian, etc. Almost none addresses the "user" constraint Clauddio raises — that treating humans only as system users ignores their full context.

**What exists on "AI leadership skills":**
C-suite focused (managing AI strategy, board governance). Almost nothing at the practitioner level — how a tech lead, senior dev, or agile coach develops leadership muscles through AI interaction.

**How this article differs:**
Every existing article in these spaces either (a) treats AI as the subject and humans as the governance mechanism, or (b) measures AI value by output. This article inverts both assumptions simultaneously. That's the positioning opportunity.

